.SH NAME
niac-list-interfaces - List available network interfaces


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac list interfaces [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List network interfaces available to NIAC. By default this shows
usable interfaces only (ethernet, Wi-Fi, and loopback). Use --all to include
every interface returned by libpcap.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	Show all interfaces instead of only usable ones

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for interfaces


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--root\fP=""
	Library root (default: NIAC_LIBRARY_ROOT or ~/.niac/library)

.PP
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # List usable interfaces
  niac list interfaces

  # Include every libpcap-visible interface
  niac list interfaces --all
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-list(1)\fP


